      "writtenOn": "2025-08-20T12:27:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So Intel marketing doesn\u0027t give \"Gen\"\u0027s anymore? It\u0027s going to be confusing to have a random \"14\" in the code. TBH the previous style seemed better.",
      "revId": "2b17a1d6ed71fdfabd4dd3b509f215e3d48cf28d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43e3ac34_93d73fc5",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/GPUInfo.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 129,
      "author": {
        "id": 3788053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-20T15:40:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Intel used to attach generation to GPUs, in addition to code names. However, this stops at Gen11, and starting from Gen12 (no more official Gen12), they call GPUs as Xe, Xe2, Xe3... (https://dgpu-docs.intel.com/devices/hardware-table.html). So 14 is not a random number, but a correct mapping to Xe3 (Xe \u003d\u003d Gen12, Xe2 \u003d\u003d Gen13).",
      "parentUuid": "2f4897cc_fe55413e",
      "revId": "2b17a1d6ed71fdfabd4dd3b509f215e3d48cf28d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8157a639_e70d179e",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/GPUInfo.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 129,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-21T07:57:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that there is a certain logic in the number you picked, but unless it matches some external known number, referring to Xe3 as \"14\" is confusing in the code. The previous helper function make it super clear what we were checking.\n\nAlternatively we could have a enum class with named generations and return that here, so the code says `if (GetIntelGen(...) \u003c\u003d IntelGen::Gen11/Xe3)`.",
      "parentUuid": "43e3ac34_93d73fc5",
      "revId": "2b17a1d6ed71fdfabd4dd3b509f215e3d48cf28d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bb1edba_1c16453d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/GPUInfo.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 129,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-22T04:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need to match the generations with number values, and the \u0027Gen\u0027 in `IntelGen` will introduce the concept of Gen13/14 again, although it is only used internally, but I\u0027d like to avoid this after Xe GPUs, and better to use the architecture names defined in `gpu_info.json` for generation detection, we just need to know Gen7,Gen8,Gen9,Gen11,Xe,Xe2,and so on. If we need more details, we already have `gpu_info::IsIntelGen12LP` and `gpu_info::IsIntelGen12HP`. \n\nFor example:\n```\nenum class IntelGen() {\n    kNonIntel \u003d 0;\n    kUnKnown \u003d 1;\n    kGen7 \u003d 7;\n    kGen8 \u003d 8;\n    ...\n    kGen11 \u003d 11;\n    kXe \u003d 12;\n    kXe2 \u003d 13;\n    kXe3 \u003d 14;\n};\n\nIntelGen GenIntelGen(PCIVendorID venderId, PCIDeviceID deviceId) {\n    gpu_info::Architecture arch \u003d gpu_info::GetArchitecture(vendorId, deviceId);\n    if (gpu_info::IsIntel(venderId) {\n        switch(arc) {\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Gen7:\n                return IntelGen::kGen7;\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Gen8:\n                return IntelGen::kGen8;\n            ...\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Gen12LP:\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Gen12HP:\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_XeLPG:\n                 return IntelGen::kXe;\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Xe2LPG:\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Xe2LHG:\n                 return IntelGen::kXe2;\n            case gpu_info::Architecture::Intel_Xe3LPG:\n                 return IntelGen::kXe3;\n            default:\n                return IntelGen::kUnKnown;\n        }\n    }\n    return IntelGen::kNonIntel;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "8157a639_e70d179e",
      "revId": "2b17a1d6ed71fdfabd4dd3b509f215e3d48cf28d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
